{
  "id": 476330070,
  "iid": 24538,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CMake: Use -Wstack-usage instead of -Wframe-larger-than",
  "description": "The latter is a greatest lower bound, the former is an upper bound.\nThey differ primarily in the treatment of alloca and VLAs. There\nare no warnings with -Wstack-usage currently, but before commit\na492f2f18944cb7b36b5b33cd3a35b606f39a1ab the use of g_alloca with\na variable produces:\n\n```c\n/home/johnthacker/git/wireshark/ui/text_import.c: In function ‘parse_seqno’:\n/home/johnthacker/git/wireshark/ui/text_import.c:1204:6: error: stack usage might be unbounded [-Werror=stack-usage=]\n 1204 | void parse_seqno(const unsigned char* start_field, const unsigned char* end_field) {\n      |      ^~~~~~~~~~~\ncc1: all warnings being treated as errors\n```\n\nCompare:\n* https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Warning-Options.html#index-Wstack-usage\n* https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Warning-Options.html#index-Wframe-larger-than_003d\n\nPing #19995\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
